      ],
      "text": "Tofacitinib for AS (adults):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 5 mg BID, or XR 11 mg QD."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "B4 starting tofacitinib, consider TB eval (active and latent), viral hepatitis screening, a CBC and updating immunizations. ⍉starting if lymphocytes <500 cells/mm³, ANC <1000 cells/mm³ or hgb <9 g/dL. Lymphocytes: baseline, then Q3M. Neutrophils: baseline, after 4-8 wks, then Q3M. Hgb: on the same schedule as neutrophils. Lipids about 4-8 wks after starting."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tofacitinib:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dose modification by indication w CYP2C19 and/or CYP3A4 inhibitors. Strong CYP3A4 inducers (ex, RIF) decrease exposure and may reduce or lose response; use together = ⍉recommended."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
